-- title:
--   Equivariant q-adic bridge and local fundamental class at w
-- statement:
--   Let $E\subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$ Galois, and let $w$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$. Write $D_w=$ `decomp E K w` for the decomposition subgroup of $K\simeq_E K$ attached to the valuation subring of the $w$-adic valuation. The assertion is that there exist a prime $q$ with $q\in w$; a finite extension $L'$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q`; an action of $D_w$ on $L'$ by semiring automorphisms which is faithful, together with a multiplicative-distributive action of $D_w$ on $(L')^{\times}$; a ring isomorphism $\Phi\colon K_w\to L'$ from the $w$-adic completion, such that $D_w$ fixes the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ pointwise, the action on units is induced by the action on $L'$, and $\Phi$ is $D_w$-equivariant; a further finite extension $K_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in the same closure which is the base of $L'$ for $D_w$, i.e. $K_0\le L'$ and an element of $L'$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by every element of $D_w$; a morphism $\theta$ of $\mathbb{Z}$-linear $D_w$-representations from the units of $L'$ (written additively) to the units of $K_w$ whose underlying map is $v\mapsto\Phi^{-1}(v)$; and a class $u\in H^2(D_w,(L')^{\times})$ satisfying `IsLocalFundamentalClass q L' D_w K₀`: for every finite extension $M\supseteq L'$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in the closure, every finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$ with normal subgroups $N_L,N_n$, an isomorphism $e\colon D_w\cong H/N_L$, an element $\varphi$ and a unit $\pi$ forming an unramified-overlay datum over $K_0$ (fixed-field descriptions of $K_0$ and $L'$, compatibility of the $D_w$- and $H$-actions through $e$, $H/N_n$ cyclic of order $|D_w|$ generated by the image of $\varphi$, $\varphi$ inducing the residue-field Frobenius, and $\pi$ an $H$-invariant uniformiser of $K_0$), and every representation morphism $\iota$ from the restriction of $(L')^{\times}$ along $e$ into $(M)^{\times}$ inducing the inclusion on elements, the image of $u$ under the map induced by $e$ and $\iota$ on $H^2$ equals the inflation from $H/N_n$ of the class of the explicit cocycle `carryFun` built from $\varphi$ and $\pi$.
--
--   This packages, at a single finite place $w$ of a finite Galois extension of number fields, the identification of the completion $K_w$ with a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ carrying the decomposition group as a faithful group of automorphisms over the fixed field $K_0$, together with the existence of the local fundamental class in $H^2(D_w,K_w^{\times})$ of local class field theory. It supplies the per-place data bound by the statement on invariant maps, [`groupCohomology.exists_isPGroup_layer_inv_eq_localInv_locRes2S_div_and_sum_inv_eq_zero_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_isPGroup_layer_inv_eq_localInv_locRes2S_div_and_sum_inv_eq_zero_of_ne_two), showing those place-by-place hypotheses to be simultaneously satisfiable.
